nguish between them to evaluate claims.\",\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"tags\": [\r\n      \"fact\",\r\n      \"opinion\",\r\n      \"critical thinking\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"mode\": \"Learn\",\r\n    \"type\": \"flashcard\",\r\n    \"options\": []\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"F616\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Reading Strategies, Critical Analysis, Reader Response, Cross-Curricular Writing, and Media Literacy\",\r\n    \"question\": \"What is Source Credibility?\",\r\n    \"answer\": \"Evaluation of an author's expertise, evidence quality, and objectivity\",\r\n    \"explanation\": \"Source Credibility considers author qualifications, evidence (research, data), objectivity, and publisher reputation. Essential for evaluating information reliability, especially online.\",\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"tags\": [\r\n      \"credibility\",\r\n      \"evaluation\",\r\n      \"sources\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"mode\": \"Learn\",\r\n    \"type\": \"flashcard\",\r\n    \"options\": []\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"F617\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Reading Strategies, Critical Analysis, Reader Response, Cross-Curricular Writing, and Media Literacy\",\r\n    \"question\": \"What is Bias?\",\r\n    \"answer\": \"A predisposition or prejudice that influences perspective or presentation of information\",\r\n    \"explanation\": \"Bias is favoritism toward one side, often unconscious. Detected through word choice, omitted information, and source selection. All texts have some bias—critical readers recognize and account for it.\",\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"tags\": [\r\n      \"bias\",\r\n      \"critical reading\",\r\n      \"perspective\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"mode\": \"Learn\",\r\n    \"type\": \"flashcard\",\r\n    \"options\": []\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"F618\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n  