uture events but isn't necessarily recurring.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q148\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Literary Analysis\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Tone reveals the author's…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Tone reveals the author's…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Mood\",\r\n      \"Attitude\",\r\n      \"Characterization\",\r\n      \"Diction\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Attitude\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Mood is the emotional atmosphere for readers, not the author's attitude.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Tone expresses the author's attitude toward the subject and audience.\",\r\n      \"Characterization develops characters, not tone.\",\r\n      \"Diction (word choice) creates tone but isn't what tone reveals.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q149\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Literary Analysis\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Mood affects the…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Mood affects the…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Reader's emotions\",\r\n      \"Author's perspective\",\r\n      \"Character's motivation\",\r\n      \"Sentence rhythm\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Reader's emotions\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Correct! Mood creates the emotional atmosphere that influences how readers feel.\",\r\n      \"Author's perspective relates to tone, not mood.\",\r\n      \"Character motivation drives plot, not mood.\",\r\n      \"Rhythm is a stylistic element, distinct from mood.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q150\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Literary Analysis\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Imagery appeals to…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Imagery appeals to…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Grammar rules\",\r\n      \"The five senses\",\r\n      \"Symbolism\",\r\n      \"Syntax\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"The five senses\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Grammar provides structure, not sensory experience.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Imagery uses descriptive language that engages sight, sound, touch, taste, and smell.\",\r\n      \"Symbolism uses objects for meaning; imagery creates sensory experience.\",\r\n      \"Syntax is sentence structure, not sensory description.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q151\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Literary Analysis\",\r\n    \"question\": \"An allegory contains…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"An allegory contains…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Only figurative language\",\r\n      \"Both literal and symbolic meanings\",\r\n      \"One simple theme\",\r\n      \"Historical facts only\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Both literal and symbolic meanings\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Allegory uses multiple literary devices, not just figurative language.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Allegory works on two levels: the surface story and its deeper symbolic meaning.\",\r\n      \"Allegories often explore complex, multi-layered themes.\",\r\n      \"While some allegories reference history, they're primarily symbolic narratives.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 3,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q152\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Literary Analysis\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Foreshadowing helps to…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Foreshadowing helps to…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Create suspense and anticipation\",\r\n      \"Summarize past events\",\r\n      \"Reveal the moral\",\r\n      \"Confuse readers intentionally\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Create suspense and anticipation\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Correct! Foreshadowing plants clues that build anticipation for future events.\",\r\n      \"Summarizing past events is exposition or flashback, not foreshadowing.\",\r\n      \"Revealing morals is the function of theme or resolution.\",\r\n      \"Good foreshadowing enhances understanding, not confusion.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q153\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Literary Analysis\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Conflict in literature functions to…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Conflict in literature functions to…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Stall character development\",\r\n      \"Create action and reveal growth\",\r\n      \"Describe setting\",\r\n      \"Provide exposition\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Create action and reveal growth\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Conflict drives development, not stalls it.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Conflict generates plot tension and forces characters to change and grow.\",\r\n      \"Setting description is separate from conflict's function.\",\r\n      \"Exposition provides background; conflict creates tension.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q154\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Literary Analysis\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Diction influences…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Diction influences…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"The story's rhyme\",\r\n      \"Tone and meaning\",\r\n      \"Theme repetition\",\r\n      \"Sentence count\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Tone and meaning\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Rhyme relates to sound patterns in poetry, not diction's primary function.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Word choice (diction) shapes both the tone and the precise meaning of the text.\",\r\n      \"Motif creates repetition, not diction itself.\",\r\n      \"Sentence count is unrelated to word choice.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q155\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Literary Analysis\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which is an example of verbal irony?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which is an example of verbal irony?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"The opposite of what's said is meant\",\r\n      \"A surprise ending\",\r\n      \"Repetition of vowel sounds\",\r\n      \"A symbol representing an idea\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"The opposite of what's said is meant\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Correct! Verbal irony occurs when someone says the opposite of what they actually mean (like sarcasm).\",\r\n      \"A surprise ending may involve situational irony, not verbal.\",\r\n      \"Repetition of vowel sounds is assonance, a sound device.\",\r\n      \"This describes symbolism, not irony.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q156\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Literary Analysis\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Symbolism helps readers…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Symbolism helps readers…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Understand literal events only\",\r\n      \"Find deeper meaning in concrete details\",\r\n      \"Track dialogue\",\r\n      \"Identify tone shifts\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Find deeper meaning in concrete details\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Symbolism adds layers beyond literal meaning.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Symbols use concrete objects to represent abstract ideas and deeper themes.\",\r\n      \"Dialogue tracking is a separate reading skill.\",\r\n      \"Tone shifts are identified through diction and style changes.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q157\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Literary Analysis\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Plot is best defined as…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Plot is best defined as…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"The message of the story\",\r\n      \"The sequence of related events\",\r\n      \"The setting's location\",\r\n      \"The author's word choice\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"The sequence of related events\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"The message is theme, not plot.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Plot is the connected series of events that make up the narrative.\",\r\n      \"Location is an element of setting.\",\r\n      \"Word choice is diction.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q158\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Literary Analysis\",\r\n    \"question\": \"The climax of a story is…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"The climax of a story is…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"The turning point or moment of greatest tension\",\r\n      \"The introduction\",\r\n      \"The falling action\",\r\n      \"The resolution\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"The turning point or moment of greatest tension\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Correct! The climax is the story's peak moment where the main conflict reaches its highest intensity.\",\r\n      \"The introduction is the exposition, beginning the story.\",\r\n      \"Falling action follows the climax, leading to resolution.\",\r\n      \"Resolution concludes the story after the climax.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q159\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Teaching and Assessment\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which is an example of formative assessment?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which is an example of formative assessment?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Final exam\",\r\n      \"Weekly quiz\",\r\n      \"Report card grade\",\r\n      \"Standardized test\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Weekly quiz\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Final exams are summative, measuring achievement at the end.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Weekly quizzes provide ongoing feedback to guide instruction during the learning process.\",\r\n      \"Report cards are summative evaluations.\",\r\n      \"Standardized tests are summative measures of overall achievement.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q160\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Teaching and Assessment\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Scaffolding helps students by…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Scaffolding helps students by…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Increasing independent learning through gradual support removal\",\r\n      \"Assigning more homework\",\r\n      \"Memorizing vocabulary lists\",\r\n      \"Focusing on spelling drills only\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Increasing independent learning through gradual support removal\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Correct! Scaffolding provides temporary support that's gradually withdrawn as students gain competence.\",\r\n      \"More homework doesn't necessarily provide structured support.\",\r\n      \"Memorization is one strategy, not scaffolding.\",\r\n      \"Spelling drills are specific practice, not the scaffolding concept.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q161\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Teaching and Assessment\",\r\n    \"question\": \"A rubric ensures…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"A rubric ensures…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Subjective grading\",\r\n      \"Consistent and transparent evaluation\",\r\n      \"Faster essay grading only\",\r\n      \"Less teacher involvement\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Consistent and transparent evaluation\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Rubrics reduce subjectivity by providing clear criteria.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Rubrics define expectations and standards, ensuring fair and consistent assessment.\",\r\n      \"While rubrics may speed grading, their main purpose is consistency and clarity.\",\r\n      \"Rubrics require thoughtful teacher design and application.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q162\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Teaching and Assessment\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Fluency in reading includes…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Fluency in reading includes…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Memorizing text\",\r\n      \"Reading with accuracy, speed, and expression\",\r\n      \"Quiet reading only\",\r\n      \"Summarizing content\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Reading with accuracy, speed, and expression\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Fluency involves decoding, not memorization.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Fluent readers demonstrate accuracy, appropriate rate, and prosody (expression).\",\r\n      \"Fluency applies to both oral and silent reading.\",\r\n      \"Summarizing demonstrates comprehension, not fluency.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q163\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Teaching and Assessment\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which stage comes first in the writing process?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which stage comes first in the writing process?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Revising\",\r\n      \"Editing\",\r\n      \"Prewriting\",\r\n      \"Publishing\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Prewriting\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Revising comes after drafting.\",\r\n      \"Editing comes near the end of the process.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Prewriting includes brainstorming, planning, and organizing ideas before drafting.\",\r\n      \"Publishing is the final stage.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q164\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Teaching and Assessment\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Metacognition involves…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Metacognition involves…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Word memorization\",\r\n      \"Monitoring one's own understanding and strategy use\",\r\n      \"Copying notes\",\r\n      \"Listening silently\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Monitoring one's own understanding and strategy use\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Memorization is a learning strategy, not metacognition.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Metacognition is awareness and regulation of one's own thinking processes.\",\r\n      \"Copying is a mechanical task without reflective thinking.\",\r\n      \"Passive listening doesn't involve metacognitive awareness.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 3,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q165\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Teaching and Assessment\",\r\n    \"question\": \"The goal of peer review is to…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"The goal of peer review is to…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Grade peers\",\r\n      \"Provide constructive feedback to improve writing\",\r\n      \"Eliminate grammar errors only\",\r\n      \"Replace teacher feedback\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Provide constructive feedback to improve writing\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Peers provide feedback, not grades.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Peer review helps writers improve through constructive, specific feedback from classmates.\",\r\n      \"While grammar matters, peer review addresses all aspects of writing.\",\r\n      \"Peer review complements, not replaces, teacher feedback.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q166\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Teaching and Assessment\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Differentiated instruction means…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Differentiated instruction means…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Teaching everyone the same way\",\r\n      \"Tailoring lessons to individual learning needs\",\r\n      \"Assigning extra credit\",\r\n      \"Reducing standards\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Tailoring lessons to individual learning needs\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Differentiation involves varying instruction, not uniformity.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Differentiated instruction adjusts teaching to meet diverse student needs, interests, and readiness levels.\",\r\n      \"Extra credit is one strategy but doesn't define differentiation.\",\r\n      \"Differentiation maintains high standards while varying approaches.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q167\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Teaching and Assessment\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Summative assessments are used to…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Summative assessments are used to…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Adjust ongoing teaching\",\r\n      \"Provide mid-unit feedback\",\r\n      \"Evaluate overall achievement at the end of instruction\",\r\n      \"Record attendance\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Evaluate overall achievement at the end of instruction\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Adjusting ongoing teaching is the purpose of formative assessment.\",\r\n      \"Mid-unit feedback is formative, not summative.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Summative assessments measure learning outcomes after instruction concludes.\",\r\n      \"Attendance tracking is administrative, not assessment.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q168\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Teaching and Assessment\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Reading conferences help teachers…\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Reading conferences help teachers…\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Punish late readers\",\r\n      \"Discuss comprehension and growth individually\",\r\n      \"Avoid grading\",\r\n      \"Assign more work\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Discuss comprehension and growth individually\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Conferences support learning, not punishment.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Reading conferences provide individualized assessment and goal-setting opportunities.\",\r\n      \"Conferences are a form of authentic assessment, not avoidance.\",\r\n      \"While teachers may assign work, the purpose is individualized support.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q301\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Rhetorical Devices and Craft Techniques\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which device repeats initial consonant sounds?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which device repeats initial consonant sounds?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Assonance\",\r\n      \"Alliteration\",\r\n      \"Consonance\",\r\n      \"Parallelism\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Alliteration\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Assonance repeats vowel sounds, not initial consonants.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Alliteration is the repetition of initial consonant sounds in neighboring words.\",\r\n      \"Consonance repeats consonant sounds at the end or middle of words.\",\r\n      \"Parallelism refers to similar grammatical structures, not sound repetition.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q302\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Rhetorical Devices and Craft Techniques\",\r\n    \"question\": \"The phrase 'The rain in Spain falls mainly on the plain' illustrates:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"The phrase 'The rain in Spain falls mainly on the plain' illustrates:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Anaphora\",\r\n      \"Assonance\",\r\n      \"Metaphor\",\r\n      \"Juxtaposition\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Assonance\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Anaphora repeats words at the beginning of clauses, not vowel sounds.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Assonance is the repetition of vowel sounds ('ai' sound) within words.\",\r\n      \"This is not a metaphor; there's no comparison being made.\",\r\n      \"Juxtaposition places contrasting elements side by side, which isn't present here.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q303\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Rhetorical Devices and Craft Techniques\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Repetition of consonant sounds at the ends of words is called:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Repetition of consonant sounds at the ends of words is called:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Chiasmus\",\r\n      \"Consonance\",\r\n      \"Alliteration\",\r\n      \"Antithesis\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Consonance\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Chiasmus is inverted parallelism, not sound repetition.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Consonance repeats consonant sounds at the end or middle of words.\",\r\n      \"Alliteration repeats initial consonant sounds, not ending sounds.\",\r\n      \"Antithesis contrasts ideas, not sound patterns.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q304\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Rhetorical Devices and Craft Techniques\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which rhetorical device repeats words at the beginning of successive clauses?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which rhetorical device repeats words at the beginning of successive clauses?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Epistrophe\",\r\n      \"Chiasmus\",\r\n      \"Anaphora\",\r\n      \"Antithesis\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Anaphora\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Epistrophe repeats words at the end of clauses, not the beginning.\",\r\n      \"Chiasmus reverses grammatical structures, not simply repeats.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Anaphora repeats words at the beginning of successive clauses.\",\r\n      \"Antithesis contrasts ideas rather than repeating words.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q305\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Rhetorical Devices and Craft Techniques\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Repetition at the end of successive clauses is called:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Repetition at the end of successive clauses is called:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Anaphora\",\r\n      \"Epistrophe\",\r\n      \"Chiasmus\",\r\n      \"Parallelism\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Epistrophe\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Anaphora repeats at the beginning, not the end.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Epistrophe repeats words at the end of successive clauses.\",\r\n      \"Chiasmus reverses structures rather than repeating at the end.\",\r\n      \"Parallelism uses similar structures but doesn't specifically repeat at the end.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q306\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Rhetorical Devices and Craft Techniques\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which example demonstrates parallel structure?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which example demonstrates parallel structure?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"She likes reading, writing, and jogging.\",\r\n      \"She likes reading and to jog.\",\r\n      \"She likes to read and jogging.\",\r\n      \"She likes reading then jog.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"She likes reading, writing, and jogging.\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\r\n    \"rationales\"