ier.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q303\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which strategy best supports students developing academic language (CALP)?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which strategy best supports students developing academic language (CALP)?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Playground talk\",\r\n      \"Scaffolded discussion using academic vocabulary\",\r\n      \"Total Physical Response\",\r\n      \"Peer imitation\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Scaffolded discussion using academic vocabulary\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Playground talk develops BICS, not CALP.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Scaffolded academic discussions with explicit vocabulary instruction build CALP.\",\r\n      \"TPR is effective for comprehension but doesn't target academic language specifically.\",\r\n      \"Peer imitation may support social language but doesn't ensure academic language development.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q304\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"A teacher gives clear examples of how to form past tense before student practice. This is:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"A teacher gives clear examples of how to form past tense before student practice. This is:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Modeling\",\r\n      \"Drilling\",\r\n      \"Code-switching\",\r\n      \"Translation\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Modeling\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Correct! Modeling demonstrates correct language use before students attempt it independently.\",\r\n      \"Drilling involves repetitive practice, not initial demonstration.\",\r\n      \"Code-switching is language alternation, not instructional demonstration.\",\r\n      \"Translation converts meaning between languages, not demonstrating form.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q305\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Pairing language commands with movement is part of:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Pairing language commands with movement is part of:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Silent Way\",\r\n      \"Direct Method\",\r\n      \"Total Physical Response\",\r\n      \"Communicative Approach\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Total Physical Response\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Silent Way minimizes teacher talk, doesn't emphasize movement.\",\r\n      \"Direct Method uses target language only, but doesn't focus on physical response.\",\r\n      \"Correct! TPR uses physical actions to reinforce language meaning and comprehension.\",\r\n      \"Communicative Approach emphasizes interaction, not specifically movement.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q306\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Waiting several seconds before calling on ELL students improves:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Waiting several seconds before calling on ELL students improves:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Grammar\",\r\n      \"Processing time\",\r\n      \"Pronunciation\",\r\n      \"Fluency\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Processing time\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Wait time doesn't directly teach grammar.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Wait time gives ELLs processing time to think, translate internally, and formulate responses.\",\r\n      \"Pronunciation requires different interventions.\",\r\n      \"While helpful, the primary benefit is processing time, not immediate fluency.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q307\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Basic Interpersonal Communication Skills (BICS) differ from CALP because they:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Basic Interpersonal Communication Skills (BICS) differ from CALP because they:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Require academic vocabulary\",\r\n      \"Develop more slowly\",\r\n      \"Are used in social settings\",\r\n      \"Depend on grammar rules\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Are used in social settings\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"BICS uses everyday vocabulary, not academic vocabulary.\",\r\n      \"BICS develops faster (1-2 years) than CALP (5-7 years).\",\r\n      \"Correct! BICS is conversational, context-embedded language used in social situations.\",\r\n      \"Both require grammar, but BICS is less formal and academic.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q308\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"When a Spanish-speaking student writes 'espectator' for 'spectator,' this reflects:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"When a Spanish-speaking student writes 'espectator' for 'spectator,' this reflects:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Language transfer\",\r\n      \"Code-switching\",\r\n      \"Fossilization\",\r\n      \"Overgeneralization\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Language transfer\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Correct! Language transfer occurs when L1 patterns influence L2 production (Spanish 'espectador' → 'espectator').\",\r\n      \"Code-switching is intentional alternation between languages, not an error.\",\r\n      \"Fossilization is persistent incorrect forms despite instruction.\",\r\n      \"Overgeneralization applies learned rules too broadly, not L1 influence.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q309\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Teachers can support second language acquisition most effectively by:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Teachers can support second language acquisition most effectively by:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Focusing only on grammar\",\r\n      \"Providing comprehensible input and context\",\r\n      \"Avoiding visuals\",\r\n      \"Limiting peer interaction\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Providing comprehensible input and context\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Grammar focus alone doesn't ensure communicative competence.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Comprehensible input with rich context supports natural acquisition.\",\r\n      \"Visuals are essential supports for ELLs.\",\r\n      \"Peer interaction builds communicative competence.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q310\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Encouraging peer collaboration and discussion builds:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Encouraging peer collaboration and discussion builds:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Morphology\",\r\n      \"Communicative competence\",\r\n      \"Syntax\",\r\n      \"Phonemic awareness\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Communicative competence\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Morphology is word structure, not built primarily through discussion.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Collaboration develops the ability to use language appropriately in social contexts.\",\r\n      \"Syntax benefits, but communicative competence is the broader outcome.\",\r\n      \"Phonemic awareness involves sound manipulation, not discussion.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q311\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"An affix attached to the beginning of a word is called a:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"An affix attached to the beginning of a word is called a:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Suffix\",\r\n      \"Prefix\",\r\n      \"Root\",\r\n      \"Stem\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Prefix\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Suffixes attach at the end.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Prefixes attach at the beginning (un-, re-, pre-).\",\r\n      \"Roots are the base meaning units.\",\r\n      \"Stems are bases to which affixes attach.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q312\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which term means an affix added to the end of a root?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which term means an affix added to the end of a root?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Prefix\",\r\n      \"Suffix\",\r\n      \"Inflection\",\r\n      \"Stem\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Suffix\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Prefixes attach at the beginning.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Suffixes attach at the end (-ness, -tion, -ly).\",\r\n      \"Inflection is a type of suffix, but suffix is the general term.\",\r\n      \"Stems are not affixes.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q313\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which suffix changes a verb to a noun?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which suffix changes a verb to a noun?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"-ize\",\r\n      \"-tion\",\r\n      \"-ful\",\r\n      \"-ous\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"-tion\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"-ize creates verbs from nouns/adjectives.\",\r\n      \"Correct! -tion creates nouns from verbs (act → action).\",\r\n      \"-ful creates adjectives from nouns.\",\r\n      \"-ous creates adjectives from nouns.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q314\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"The suffix '-ize' typically forms:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"The suffix '-ize' typically forms:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Nouns\",\r\n      \"Verbs\",\r\n      \"Adjectives\",\r\n      \"Adverbs\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Verbs\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Nouns are formed by -tion, -ness, -ment.\",\r\n      \"Correct! -ize forms verbs (modern → modernize).\",\r\n      \"Adjectives use -ful, -ous, -able.\",\r\n      \"Adverbs use -ly.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q315\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"The suffix '-ous' turns a noun into an:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"The suffix '-ous' turns a noun into an:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Adjective\",\r\n      \"Verb\",\r\n      \"Adverb\",\r\n      \"Pronoun\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Adjective\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Correct! -ous creates adjectives (danger → dangerous).\",\r\n      \"-ize, -en, -ify create verbs.\",\r\n      \"-ly typically creates adverbs.\",\r\n      \"Pronouns are not formed with suffixes.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q316\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which classroom activity best supports morphological awareness?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which classroom activity best supports morphological awareness?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Memorizing spelling lists\",\r\n      \"Sorting words by affixes\",\r\n      \"Copying sentences\",\r\n      \"Reciting rhymes\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Sorting words by affixes\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Memorization doesn't build awareness of word structure.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Sorting by affixes helps students analyze and understand word parts.\",\r\n      \"Copying doesn't emphasize morphological analysis.\",\r\n      \"Rhymes support phonological awareness, not morphological.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q317\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which morpheme type changes word meaning but not grammatical role?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which morpheme type changes word meaning but not grammatical role?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Inflectional\",\r\n      \"Derivational\",\r\n      \"Compound\",\r\n      \"Bound root\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Derivational\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Inflectional morphemes indicate grammar (tense, number) without changing meaning.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Derivational morphemes create new words and meanings (happy → happiness).\",\r\n      \"Compounds combine two words, not morphemes.\",\r\n      \"Bound roots don't change meaning, they carry core meaning.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q318\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Adding '-ed' to indicate past tense is an example of a:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Adding '-ed' to indicate past tense is an example of a:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Derivational morpheme\",\r\n      \"Inflectional morpheme\",\r\n      \"Prefix\",\r\n      \"Suffix root\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Inflectional morpheme\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Derivational morphemes change word class or meaning.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Inflectional morphemes mark grammar (tense, number, comparison) without changing word class.\",\r\n      \"Prefixes attach at the beginning.\",\r\n      \"This is an inflectional suffix, not a root.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q319\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Students comparing English and Spanish word endings practice:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Students comparing English and Spanish word endings practice:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Syntax\",\r\n      \"Metalinguistic awareness\",\r\n      \"Fluency\",\r\n      \"Phonology\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Metalinguistic awareness\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Syntax is sentence structure, not word analysis.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Metalinguistic awareness is consciously thinking about language structures.\",\r\n      \"Fluency is speed and accuracy, not language analysis.\",\r\n      \"Phonology is sound systems, not morphology.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q320\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"A classroom focused on conversation, gestures, and visual aids demonstrates:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"A classroom focused on conversation, gestures, and visual aids demonstrates:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Grammar-Translation\",\r\n      \"Communicative approach\",\r\n      \"Audio-lingual method\",\r\n      \"Direct method\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Communicative approach\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Grammar-Translation emphasizes written translation and explicit grammar.\",\r\n      \"Correct! The Communicative approach emphasizes meaningful interaction and context.\",\r\n      \"Audio-lingual method focuses on drills and repetition.\",\r\n      \"Direct method uses target language only, without emphasizing visuals/gestures as much.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q321\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Teachers lower the affective filter by:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Teachers lower the affective filter by:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Increasing test frequency\",\r\n      \"Creating a supportive environment\",\r\n      \"Correcting every error publicly\",\r\n      \"Reducing peer interaction\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Creating a supportive environment\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Frequent testing can raise anxiety.\",\r\n      \"Correct! A supportive, low-anxiety environment lowers the affective filter and promotes acquisition.\",\r\n      \"Public correction raises anxiety.\",\r\n      \"Peer interaction supports language development.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q322\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Development, Second Language Acquisition, and Word Formation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Providing sentence frames such as 'I think ___ because ___' helps students:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Providing sentence frames such as 'I think ___ because ___' helps students:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Build syntax and academic discourse\",\r\n      \"Pract