 Language, Borrowings, and Regional Variation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which of the following best defines 'dialect'?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which of the following best defines 'dialect'?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"A social language register\",\r\n      \"A simplified communication form\",\r\n      \"A regional or social language variety\",\r\n      \"A new language created from two others\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"A regional or social language variety\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Register refers to formality level, not dialect.\",\r\n      \"This describes pidgin, not dialect.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Dialects are systematic regional or social varieties of a language.\",\r\n      \"This describes a creole or mixed language.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q335\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Development of English Language, Borrowings, and Regional Variation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"An individual's unique way of speaking is referred to as their:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"An individual's unique way of speaking is referred to as their:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Sociolect\",\r\n      \"Dialect\",\r\n      \"Idiolect\",\r\n      \"Register\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Idiolect\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Sociolect is group-based, not individual.\",\r\n      \"Dialect is regional/social, not individual.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Idiolect is an individual's unique linguistic fingerprint.\",\r\n      \"Register is formality level, not individual style.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q336\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Development of English Language, Borrowings, and Regional Variation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Language associated with specific social groups or classes is called a:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Language associated with specific social groups or classes is called a:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Pidgin\",\r\n      \"Sociolect\",\r\n      \"Dialect\",\r\n      \"Register\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Sociolect\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Pidgin is a contact language, not a social variety.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Sociolect reflects social class, education, or group membership.\",\r\n      \"Dialect is regional, not specifically social.\",\r\n      \"Register is formality level.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q337\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Development of English Language, Borrowings, and Regional Variation\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which statement best defines slang?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which statement best defines slang?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"A fixed formal register\",\r\n      \"A type of professional jargon\",\r\n      \"Informal language used for identity or novelty\",\r\n      \"Words borrowed from Latin\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Informal language used for identity or novelty\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Slang is informal, not formal.\",\r\n      \"Jargon is specialized; slang is broader and more informal.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Slang is informal, group-specific, and evolves rapidly.\",\r\n      \"Latin borrowings are not necessarily slang.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q338\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Development of English Language, Borrowings, and 