rary Response, and Expository Writing Techniques\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which choice best signals a shift in tone that creates ironic undertones?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which choice best signals a shift in tone that creates ironic undertones?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Literal description only\",\r\n      \"Exaggerated praise of a clearly flawed subject\",\r\n      \"Chronological exposition\",\r\n      \"Objective reporting\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Exaggerated praise of a clearly flawed subject\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Literal description lacks the contrast needed for irony.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Exaggerating praise of something flawed creates verbal irony—saying opposite of what's meant.\",\r\n      \"Chronological structure doesn't create irony.\",\r\n      \"Objective reporting avoids ironic tone.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q409\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Structure, Literary Response, and Expository Writing Techniques\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Dialogue that reveals a character's values is primarily an example of:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Dialogue that reveals a character's values is primarily an example of:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Plot structure\",\r\n      \"Characterization\",\r\n      \"Setting detail\",\r\n      \"Foreshadowing\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Characterization\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Plot is sequence of events, not character revelation.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Characterization methods include dialogue revealing personality, beliefs, and values.\",\r\n      \"Setting is time/place, not character traits.\",\r\n      \"Foreshadowing hints at future events, not character values.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 1,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \