ect! Universal themes address fundamental human experiences that transcend culture and time.\",\r\n      \"Regional dialect is specific, not universal.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q412\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Structure, Literary Response, and Expository Writing Techniques\",\r\n    \"question\": \"The strongest thesis statement is typically:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"The strongest thesis statement is typically:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Vague and broad\",\r\n      \"A factual statement\",\r\n      \"A clear, arguable claim with scope\",\r\n      \"A rhetorical question\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"A clear, arguable claim with scope\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Vague, broad statements lack focus and arguability.\",\r\n      \"Facts aren't arguable—strong theses present debatable positions.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Strong theses are clear, arguable, specific, and provide direction for the essay.\",\r\n      \"Questions don't assert positions—they invite inquiry.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q413\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Structure, Literary Response, and Expository Writing Techniques\",\r\n    \"question\": \"Which organizational pattern is best for evaluating two pedagogical models?\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which organizational pattern is best for evaluating two pedagogical models?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Chronological\",\r\n      \"Definition\",\r\n      \"Compare–contrast\",\r\n      \"Process analysis\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Compare–contrast\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Chronological shows time sequence, not evaluatio