:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"In contemporary linguistics, the term World Englishes refers to:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"Attempts to restore classical grammar in global education\",\r\n      \"Localized varieties of English shaped by regional and cultural factors\",\r\n      \"The replacement of native languages with English worldwide\",\r\n      \"Simplified English used exclusively in diplomacy\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"answer\": \"Localized varieties of English shaped by regional and cultural factors\",\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"World Englishes recognizes diversity, not restoration of classical grammar.\",\r\n      \"Correct! 'World Englishes' recognizes that British, Indian, Nigerian, and Singaporean English are all legitimate, evolving varieties.\",\r\n      \"The term celebrates multilingualism, not language replacement.\",\r\n      \"World Englishes includes all varieties, not just simplified diplomatic English.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2,\r\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\r\n    \"type\": \"mcq\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q643\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Understanding the purposes and values of teaching literature\",\r\n    \"question\": \"A teacher organizes a literature unit including The Joy Luck Club by Amy Tan, Bless Me, Ultima by Rudolfo Anaya, and The Namesake by Jhumpa Lahiri. The teacher's primary purpose in selecting these works is to:\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"A teacher organizes a literature unit including The Joy Luck Club by Amy Tan, Bless Me, Ultima by Rudolfo Anaya, and The Namesake by Jhumpa Lahiri. The teacher's primary purpose in selecting these works is to:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\r\n      \"expose students to novels written exclusively in first person.\",\r\n      \"highlight the influence of myth and folklore in contemporary fiction.\",\r\n      \"explore the experiences of cultural identity and assimilation in 